    "Touching a grip holds its assigned key or mouse button; releasing it releases that action. This senses hand contact, not squeeze pressure. A grip can also activate gyro aiming.": {
      "comment": "Controller sensor settings, calibration guidance, or information popover.",
      "extractionState": "manual"
    },
    "Gyro aiming turns controller rotation into mouse movement. Choose a touch to activate it, or Always. Save & Apply changes before enabling output. Keep the controller still for calibration. With touch activation, release the control after enabling output, then touch again to aim. Calibrate Again resets sensor bias without changing your mappings; it requires active output, fresh motion data and no profile operation in progress.": {
      "comment": "Controller sensor settings, calibration guidance, or information popover.",
      "extractionState": "manual"
    },
